## What was fixed

The current AT Protocol OAuth requirements were applied from the [AT Protocol OAuth specification](https://atproto.com/specs/oauth): authorization-code flow, PKCE S256, PAR, DPoP, issuer binding, refresh-token [REDACTED], and exact callback validation.

The PDS now has an optional, test-only short-token-lifetime configuration:

- [`env.ts`](/var/home/tcs/Code/atproto/upstream/atproto-pds/packages/pds/src/config/env.ts:32) reads `PDS_OAUTH_TOKEN_MAX_AGE_MS`.
- [`config.ts`](/var/home/tcs/Code/atproto/upstream/atproto-pds/packages/pds/src/config/config.ts:328) rejects non-positive values and passes the setting into the OAuth provider.
- [`context.ts`](/var/home/tcs/Code/atproto/upstream/atproto-pds/packages/pds/src/context.ts:380) wires the configured lifetime into the provider.
- [`config.test.ts`](/var/home/tcs/Code/atproto/upstream/atproto-pds/packages/pds/tests/config.test.ts:1) verifies the configured, default, and invalid-value cases.
- The default remains unchanged when the environment variable is unset.

The credentialed OAuth runner at [`credentialed_public_oauth.mjs`](/var/home/tcs/Code/atproto/scripts/credentialed_public_oauth.mjs:1) now:

- creates only disposable identities;
- supports an isolated local loopback PDS;
- starts a temporary local callback listener;
- uses exact callback origin and path matching;
- avoids logging callback query parameters, codes, tokens, cookies, passwords, or DPoP material;
- proves pre-expiry access;
- waits for the short-lived access token to expire;
- proves stale access-token [REDACTED];
- proves refresh success and refresh-token [REDACTED];
- rejects replay of the old refresh token;
- rejects authorization-code replay;
- proves authorization-code replay invalidates the resulting session;
- performs cleanup and revocation.

I also changed the public runner guard so an explicitly opted-in HTTPS staging subdomain under the existing `edriffles.us` zone is allowed. It requires explicit issuer and handle-domain bindings, so the test does not accidentally run against the live PDS. No `radlib.org` requirement was added.

The new external evidence contract is implemented in [`validate_external_gate_receipts.py`](/var/home/tcs/Code/atproto/scripts/validate_external_gate_receipts.py:1). It validates:

- secret-free Relay/AppView canary receipts;
- source, image, environment, and timestamp bindings;
- positive control-canary observations;
- negative private-canary observations;
- short-TTL OAuth expiry and replay checks;
- PLC operator identity and endpoint separation;
